Aerie-Purpose: Keep the Tab Model record id from a restored tab's extra data on the tab, so the tab strip adapter can join the tab to its record.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui (browser_tabrestore.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #223. chrome::AddRestoredTab already passes the tab's session extra data to
glic::RestoreGlicStateFromExtraData and SendTabToSelfActivationTracker::RestoreFromExtraData before
the tab goes into its strip. It now also calls aerie_tab_model::StashRestoredRecordId (overlay,
chrome/browser/aerie_tab_model/session_record_id_hook.h). The call keeps a well-formed record id
(1 to 64 characters of A-Z a-z 0-9 - _) as user data on the WebContents and ignores anything else;
TabStripAdapter::TabInserted reads it and forgets it. The value comes from the session file on disk
and is only looked up in the Tab Model, never used as an index. The header has no dependencies, so
the new dep of browser_tabrestore_impl cannot make a cycle.

